Z||000000||bubbajoexx||12-04-2000||07:50 PM||||I have looked at about 20 V8 conversions all of them 350 chev they were all to expencive or did to much body mods and I don't like cutting the frame or fender wells so iImade my own I put a 4.5 caddy aluminium V8 in mine it is great it may not have 300 foot pounds of torque but 220 is fine by me and 240 hp works just fine and it don't sound like awounded duck 6 so has any one elts tried it bubbajoexx||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||12-04-2000||08:29 PM||||Whoa, that's one helluva run-on sentence! I think the Cadillac 4.5/4.9 is a great swap. 200hp and 275ft/lb without any more weight than a 2.8 V6. I have a 4.1 (135hp 180ft/lb)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> sitting in my Rossa chassis, and a 4.9 waiting to replace it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> . I don't think your 4.5 makes 240hp unless it's been worked over.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Formula 18||12-04-2000||09:02 PM||||I think this would make a great swap too, but what trannys are you guys running and what about a flywheel???<P>bubbajoexx-<BR>Did you put it in transverse? I'd like to know what kind of mounts you are using and how did you rout the exhaust? Also how much rooms is left in the engine compartment?? Enough for Twin T-3's??? <P>Brian <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||bubbajoexx||12-05-2000||12:01 PM||||I am using the stock fiero trans axle. I build my own mounts . Email me on the mounts for more info.The Canadian 4.5 dose make 240 hp because of the diferance in emision standards and the9.5:1 compression ratio where as the us engine is 8.5 :1 compression. And yes the engine is transverse (By the way you must use an aftermarket mini starter for fiero transaxle use)           bubbajoexx||||reg||1
